## Sass Overview

Sass is compiled by the Dart Sass compiler (the current official implementation) into plain CSS.

## Two Syntaxes

```sass
// .sass (indented — no braces or semicolons)
.button
  background: blue
  &:hover
    background: darkblue
```

```scss
// .scss (superset of CSS — most common)
.button {
  background: blue;
  &:hover { background: darkblue; }
}
```

## Core Features

```scss
// @use — module system (replaces @import)
@use 'sass:math';
@use 'tokens' as t;

// Variables
$spacing-4: 1rem;

// Mixins with arguments
@mixin respond-to($bp) {
  @media (min-width: $bp) { @content; }
}

.hero {
  padding: $spacing-4;
  @include respond-to(768px) { padding: $spacing-4 * 2; }
}

// @extend — share a set of declarations
%visually-hidden {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip-path: inset(50%);
}
.sr-only { @extend %visually-hidden; }
```

## Current Status

Sass is still widely used in large codebases and UI libraries. However, many modern projects favour CSS custom properties + PostCSS or Tailwind, which reduce the need for a full preprocessor.

